Package: PhyloPCA
Title: Phylogenetic Signal in Continuous, Discrete and Geometric-Morphometric
    Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Martin R.", "Smith",
           email = "martin.smith@durham.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5660-1727"))
Description: Simulates continuous, discrete and geometric-morphometric
    ('shape') character data on a fixed generative tree, and reconstructs
    phylogeny from each using neighbour-joining, maximum parsimony and
    Bayesian inference, so that reconstruction accuracy can be compared
    across data types and methods. Provides the simulation, alignment,
    tree-inference and scoring functions, together with the cached results,
    underlying Smith (2026), a reply to Raskin et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.1002/ajpa.70306> on whether principal components analysis can
    recover phylogenetic signal from continuous morphological data.
